A||N||23||fropuff||Another speaker question...||||5||
Z||000000||fropuff||11-21-2000||07:29 PM||||As you may know, I got some 4"s for the front dash on my 86 GT.  I like these speakers, and I was wondering if I could take them out for now, and put them in my Cutlass in the 3.5" space.  I don't really care if it does anything to my speakers, as I have the 4 year service plan from Best Buy.  Will this work if I do it?  Thanks.<P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters are for those who are worried about being caught.||||reg||5
Z||000001||fropuff||11-21-2000||10:28 PM||||I also forgot something...I didn't mean that I would use all of the 4s in the 3.5 space.  You probably figured it out yourselves anyway.  I would just use two.  I wouldn't care if I had to cut a little; I'm drilling a big 1" hole in the fender tomorrow for my antenna.  That's why I need to know if I can pull it off.  I want to get everything set for February 13th, 2001.  (Already planning ahead.)  I also need to know how to wire.  I would guess + to + and - to -, huh?  Can someone please help me out?  Thanks a lot.<P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters are for those who are worried about being caught.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Seanh||11-21-2000||10:45 PM||||That will be fine. Like you said, you will have to do some cutting to get them in there, but it will work. If I recall correctly I think we have put some 5.25" Speakers in a Cutlass once. + to + and - to -. Do you know which is which on the Cutlass? If not, you should look on the net to find the color coding. What year Cutlass is it? We have some books here, but they dont go back very far. We are in the process of changing over to a computer based system for all the wiring information on cars, so were a little unorganized.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/transsig.gif">  <BR><A HREF="http://www.kdsi.net/~sean" TARGET=_blank>Sean's Fiero Page</A><BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8 Auto<BR>Going on to 3.4 in Jan.<BR><I>"If you smoke after sex, you're doing it way to fast".</I>||||reg||1
Z||000003||fropuff||11-22-2000||08:02 PM||||Thanks for the help.  It's a 1980 Cutlass.  I don't know what the wire colors are, but it should say on the back of the speaker what is + and -.  I'm glad I can put the 4s in there.  I only have one working of the two I have, and I have NO bass at all.  I'm going to get some 4x10s for the rear deck sometime.  I will have to cut, but it doesn't matter.  Thanks again.<P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters are for those who are worried about being caught.||||reg||1
Z||000004||fropuff||11-24-2000||07:19 PM||||Well, I got the 4s in yesterday and the antenna in today.  I screwed up on both parts.  I didn't "screw" up the speakers, but I don't think it's worth it to keep them in there.  They don't sound as good as in the Fiero, so I'm going to get some cheap 3 1/2s tomorrow.  I'm probably not going to get some "good" sound from that little a speaker anyway.  I also busted up the brittle dash board trying to get the covers out.  The colors were the same as the Fiero.  Light greeen and dark green for the right, brown and gray for the left.  It was easy to figure it out that way.  Anyway, as the antenna screw-up goes, I found out why the windshield antenna didn't work.  Turns out it came unplugged from the AM a while ago when I was moving it around, so I just figured it was bad.  I didn't even bother putting it back in.  So I already had a 3/4" hole in the left fender when I found the original plug.  I figured I'd try it out, so I plugged it in and turned the FM on.  IT worked, but not as good as the antenna kit, so I didn't screw up that much.  $8 isn't bad anyway.  I have ANOTHER question though.  I want to get some 4x10s for the rear deck, maybe some Pioneers?  It doesn't matter what kind.  I want to know how I would wire them up.  Do I wire them to the FM or to the 3 1/2s or what?  Some detailed instructions would be greatly appreciated.  Thanks a lot for the help.  <P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters are for those who are worried about being caught.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Seanh||11-24-2000||07:49 PM||||Yeah, you really wont get good sound from 4" speakers alone. They are only good for mid-bass. Combinded with subs and tweeter, they would be the best. As for doing the 4x10's in the rear deck. Does the car already have speakers back there, or provisions for speakers back there? If it does'nt, then I would reccomend going the 6x9 rount instead of 4x10. If it does have the 4x10 hols, then you can get adapter plates to mount 6x9's in the 4x10 holes. 6x9 IMO would sound alot better. Those Pioneer 4-ways are the best. If the car has rear speakers already, then you just wire them up like you did the front speakers. If it doesnt have speakers, and doesnt have wires for them, then, if you are useing the stock headunit, you will probally have to wire into the front speaker outputs. I would think even the stock headunit would have rear speaker outputs. If you are useing aftermarket unit, then it does have rear speaker outputs. If the wires are not already ran to the back, you will have to run speaker wires to the rear speakers yourself. If they are already there, then you just need to hook up the speakers.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/transsig.gif">  <BR><A HREF="http://www.kdsi.net/~sean" TARGET=_blank>Sean's Fiero Page</A><BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8 Auto<BR>Going on to 3.4 in Jan.<BR><I>"If you smoke after sex, you're doing it way to fast".</I>||||reg||1
Z||000006||fropuff||11-24-2000||07:53 PM||||I think I understand.  I already have the cutouts for the 4x10s on the rear deck; I know that some 6x9s won't fit, too wide.  I believe the head unit (it's the stock one) has a rear speaker output.  It's got the selector to fade from front to rear.  I guess the output must be there.  It doesn't have wiring, though, as there weren't any there in the first place.  So, what should I do about them?  Thanks a lot.<P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters are for those who are worried about being caught.||||reg||1
Z||000007||batboy||11-24-2000||10:14 PM||||Those stock head units can really only handle one speaker per channel. If it has a fader and balance controls both, then you should have front and rear stereo, or 4 channels. In that case, you can safely hook up 4 speakers. Too bad you couldn't get the 4" speakers to work in the front, they're better than 3-1/2" ones in my opinion. You'll need to run two pairs of speaker wires from the head unit to the rear. Tuck them under the door sill (you'll have to remove the trim, usually not hard) and under the back seat, then up through the trunk to the rear shelf. Wire them the same as the front (+ to + etc.).||||reg||1
Z||000008||fropuff||11-24-2000||11:21 PM||||Thanks for the help.  I did get the 4s to work, and they sound pretty good, but I want a pair to keep in the Cutlass.  I busted up the dash pretty bad trying to get the covers off, and I don't want to cut anything to get the 4s in.  As far as the rear speakers go, where do I find the output for the rear speakers?  So I run two sets of wires through to the rear, one on each side?  So each side would have a + and a -?  I'll look tomorrow at the rear of the unit.  Thanks again.  ||||reg||1
Z||000009||fropuff||11-24-2000||11:25 PM||||Okay, I went out and got the old AM radio.  It's the same as the FM; just doesn't have FM.  I've got three plugs on the rear of the unit, and I used two.  I used the one on the left side and the center one; I guess the third is for the rear speakers?  Where would I go to find a plug that will fit this vehicle?  Thanks a lot.<P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters are for those who are worried about being caught.||||reg||1
Z||000010||Seanh||11-24-2000||11:25 PM||||Just have to run the wire to the rear deck then. They make special adapters to mount 6x9's in 4x10 holes. They mount under the deck and center the speaker in the hole. It would seem like they wounldnt sound good because the speaker is somewhat covered up, but they sound just as good as any 4x10 youll ever get. As for brands, I would highly reccomend Pioneer. They are one of the best you can get. Sony X-Plod's are nice also, along with Infinity and Kenwood. I would reccomend going the 6x9 route. Is there enough space to mount 6x9's under the deck? If there is then I can get you the kit to do it. Off the top of my head I am thinking it is about $24.00 for the pair to mount 6x9's under the deck. I can also get the Pioneer 6x9 4-ways for about $129.00 I think. They sound awesome.||||reg||1
Z||000011||fropuff||11-24-2000||11:30 PM||||No, there is not enough room to adapt to a 6x9.  It's about 5" wide, underneath and on top.  Same each way.  There's about a 1/2" left on each side of the cutout.  I might try something out.  Now, the wiring:  I just get a new plug with two sets of wiring, one goes on each side?  I see on the bottom of the unit, there's a diagram:<P>+RR      RR-<BR>+LR      LR-<BR>+LF      LF-<BR>+RF      RF-<BR> LAMP    ANT<BR> GRD     12V+<P>I think I know what these markings mean, I just thought they'd help a little.  Any ideas?  Thanks a lot.<P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters are for those who are worried about being caught.||||reg||1
Z||000012||Seanh||11-24-2000||11:36 PM||||I dont understand what you are saying about the plugs on the headunit. How many wires are going to these plugs? A picture would be great if you happen to have a digital cam handy. All headunits have the same basic wires. 4 Speaker outputs (+ & - for each one), Power, Ingition switched power) Ground, Auto on Lead (power antenna's), and an Antenna input. That should give you around 12 wires. I would guess that one plug has 3 or 4 wires in it, and has Power, Ignition switch power, Ground, and maybe the antenna-on lead. The other one probally has the 2 front speaker outputs, + and - for each one. And the last plug probally has the read speaker outputs (+ and - for each one). Sounds like this is what you unit is like. any ideas? Hope this helps.||||reg||1
Z||000013||fropuff||11-24-2000||11:40 PM||||I don't know what I'm talking about, but I would guess that the third plug would be used for the rear speakers.  As far as the "three plugs" go, there is about 12 wires going to the two.  There probably would be about 4 going to the other one.  I hope I'm not bothering you; you've all been a big help.  Thanks a lot.||||reg||1
Z||000014||Seanh||11-24-2000||11:42 PM||||Okay, I know how it is working then. I am sure you understand the speaker markings right? The "Lamp" marking, that turns on the illumination for the radio whenever your headlights or fog lamps are on. The GND is the ground. The 12+ is the power to run the unit, I would guess it is ingition switched. ANT is the auto-on lead for a power antenna. Hope this will help. You should be able to get a factory replacment harness and just use the one plug from it, it will plug into the harness comming from the stereo. Or, you can just cut the harness off the stereo and splic into the wires. ||||reg||1
Z||000015||Seanh||11-24-2000||11:46 PM||||Yes, the third plug is going to be for the rear speakers. You could tell which wires comming from the stereo are the correct ones to hook to the speaker and to which side they go, by looking at the other plugs and seeing which are which from there. I would assume that the diagram is the same direction as the plugs and gives you a general idea as to which wires are which.||||reg||1
Z||000016||fropuff||11-24-2000||11:47 PM||||Thanks.  So I can get a wiring harness that will go into the third plug?  Should there be four wires coming out of it?  If I understand correctly, it should be about the same as the front?  Thanks again for the help.<p>[This message has been edited by fropuff (edited 11-24-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000017||Seanh||11-25-2000||12:02 AM||||Well, you can get a set of the 3 harness's that plug into the stereo, you cant just buy the one by itself, you will have to get all three. Just go to a stereo shop or some place that sells car harness and tell them you want the "Factory Replacment" harness. It is the harness that plugs into the back of the stock headunit. They will probally have it, or can order it.||||reg||1
Z||000018||fropuff||11-25-2000||12:05 AM||||NOW I understand.  Lucky for you.  I just didn't understand about the wiring thing.  I might just go out and find some, then just use the one.  No sense cutting all the wires when I don't have to.  I'm not doing the 4x10s now, but I want to know what I need, if I have to order it.  Thanks a bunch.<P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters are for those who are worried about being caught.||||reg||1
Z||000019||fropuff||01-28-2001||04:38 PM||||Okay, I went to Best Buy and bought two wiring harnesses for 78-90 GMs.  Got 'em home, and neither of them will work.  The thing I need is not the wiring harness itself, but the "plug" that goes into the wiring harness.  I actually don't even need a harness.  That's already in the back of the stock radio.  Where can I find this "plug" for the rear speakers?  Do I need to take a radio out and pull the plug out from a Cutlass at the salvage yard?  Thanks.<P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters are for those who are worried about being caught.||||reg||1
Z||000020||fropuff||01-28-2001||04:41 PM||||BTW: I don't know if this matters, but the wiring colors on the plug are Green and Violet, for rear right and rear left.  Thanks again for the help.  ||||reg||1
Z||000021||Seanh||01-28-2001||09:18 PM||||Are you lookin' for the plug to go into the rear speakers? Chances are slim to nothin' that your going to find those anywhere but a junk/salvage yard. If I were you, I would just cut them off, with as much wire as you can spare, wire your new speakers up to the wires on the car directly and use them. When your ready to switch back, if you ever want to, wire the connector back up to the car wires and plug the old spearkers back in.||||reg||1
Z||000022||fropuff||01-28-2001||11:45 PM||||Okay, now I get it, again.  The thing I need is the plug for the rear speaker output on the radio.  I guess I'll just go to the junk yard, get the plug, get some wire, get some speakers, put the speakers in the rear deck, put the plug in the radio, and run the wire from the plug to the speakers.  I think this is right.  Thanks a lot for the help.  That's all I wanted to know; I need to learn how to specify.  Thanks a lot.||||reg||1
Z||000023||fropuff||02-03-2001||06:21 PM||||My speaker questions are now over!  I just went to the salvage yard today and got the plug for the rear speakers that goes into the radio.  I also got some Pioneer 6x9 speakers at Wal Mart for $30!  That's why I got them; they were cheap.  I just temporarily wired them up to hear them, and there's definately a difference.  More bass!  I might get some bass blockers for the front 3.5s.  I'm going to wire them up tomorrow; getting dark now.  I would like to thank everyone that helped me out.  Thanks!  I'll let you know what they sound like tomorrow.  Thanks again!!<P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters are for those who are worried about being caught.||||reg||1
